## Earliest remaining R2 producer

The new directed-wedge permutation contracts mostly pass, but valid source-boundary, disconnected-component, singularity-fan, interior-hard-rail, and periodic-cylinder sectors are omitted from the final `auditedCycles` and cell inventory.

Evidence:

- valid halfedges retain `cell == -1`;
- planar Euler is `-1`, area error is `1`, and no exterior boundary cycle is emitted;
- disconnected components produce zero interior cells;
- interior hard rail creates two exterior classifications;
- bunny singularity fan produces zero center cells instead of three;
- cylinder reports `invalid-cell cell=-1 halfedge=0 twin=1 next=4`;
- seam, close sheets, and cylinder produce zero arrangement cells and fail `SideSubdivisionRepair:InvalidInputIncidence`;
- eight Phase 17 contracts are preempted by absent/invalid arrangement cells.

Plane still reaches 12 completed quads and 15 aggregate validation failures. Seam and close sheets regress from later completion/output validation to zero cells/quads. Do not advance to R3 while R2 remains causal.

